==============================================================================
O12 — dyadic block ratio  rho = r_2N / r_N   (fit-free)
==============================================================================
  Delta_N = sum over primes[N:2N] of p^(-sigma) exp(-i t log p)
  r_N     = |Delta_N| / N
  rho     = r_2N / r_N ;  a = 1 + log2(rho)
  landmarks: a=1 -> rho=1.00000000 ;  a=1/2 -> rho=0.70710678
  no least squares, no r^2, no window, no fitted threshold

!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
KNOWN DESIGN FLAW IN THE DECISION RULE — read before the tables
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
  The ADD and SQRT bands COINCIDE at sigma = 0.5.  The additive law
  a = 1 - sigma gives a = 1/2 there, which is numerically identical
  to square-root cancellation.  A SQRT verdict at sigma = 0.5 is NOT
  evidence of cancellation.  sigma = 0 is the DISCRIMINATING row:
  additive predicts rho = 1.0 there and sqrt-cancellation predicts
  rho = 0.70710678, which the rule can separate.
